      "content": "Religious conservatives generally argue against medical aid in dying, often based on the belief in the inherent sanctity of life, which they believe is a divine gift that should not be intentionally ended. This perspective strongly emphasizes the absolute value of human life, regardless of its perceived quality or the individual's suffering.\n\nIn contrast, religious liberals often advocate for the right to choose in end-of-life care, arguing that personal autonomy and the compassionate care for a loved one are moral priorities. They frequently support the right to die with dignity, framing the issue through a lens of love and individual liberty within a religious framework.",
