      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's helpful. i see you're using terms like 'deontological natural law' for the conservative side, but for the liberal side you're talking about 'nuanced interpretations' and 'dignity of the whole person.' it almost feels like the conservative view is just a rigid set of rules, while the liberal view is more of an evolving, compassionate response to real human suffering. \n\ncan you explain why the conservative framework is often criticized for being so rigid in this regard? i want to make sure i understand the critique of their logic so i can address it in my thesis.",
